# Ramp6Control + CheckMode15Start, HELD-BALL case (companion of dc_flurry.uh, the free-ball case): dragon lights 22-25 and 27 lit, a_ramp6 lights v_lite26 -> flurry (mode 15, multiball +3, text 3063, sound tabc61wave id 49).
# With the ball still on the plunger the flurry adds +3 (the free-ball +4 is dc_flurry.uh). NewGame starts in mode 10 with the ball on the plunger (ball_held 1, as Wine's
# first sample after NewGame); Mode15Controller (dragon_core.cpp) adds 4 and takes 1 back when S().BallHeld != 0
# (original 0x42b510), then relaunches the held ball. The precondition line: expect ball_held == 1.
init window 960 666
init fixed_dt 10
init seed 1
init watch v_lite70.light_on
10 key down new_game
11 key up new_game
190 poke info_text_box message_field 2
195 poke v_lite22 light_on 1
195 poke v_lite23 light_on 1
195 poke v_lite24 light_on 1
195 poke v_lite25 light_on 1
195 poke v_lite27 light_on 1
200 event a_ramp6 ControlBallToLayer2
205 expect mode == 15
199 expect ball_held == 1
205 expect multiball == 3 delta 199
195-205 expect text info_text_box display id 3063
195-205 expect sound 49
205 expect v_lite70.light_on == 1
250 quit
